A||||6||Brandon86SE||Interior Courtesy Lights||||1||
Z||000000||Brandon86SE||09-19-2001||12:48 AM||||I decided today that it was time for a change with my interior, and a nice, cheap thing to do was change the colour of the courtesy (open door) lights.  I decided on red, to match with my park lights on the gauges.  So I ripped out every interior light except the map lights, which I will leave white.  I was able to find red bulbs for the footwell bulbs, and lighter bulb.  I decided to just leave the lighter unlit though, 'cause I never use it anyway.  However, I was unable to find the bulbs for the little ashtray bulbs (which I might just leave pulled as well), or the dome light.  The footwells look amazing, but the bright white coming out of the dome lights just doesn't work right now.  Does anyone know of a place (Canadian) that has these size bulbs?  I was told they were a "904" bulb.  I already tried Canadian Tire, and PartSource.  I'm gonna try AutoZeal tomorrow, they might, but I doubt this bulb is on any foreign cars.  What I was really wondering is whether you guys think it would be safe to put the same bulbs from the footwells into the dome.  They appear to have the same connection, and are both 12V.  I didn't think of this 'till just now, so they might not have quite the same connection, but if I recall it was quite close.  Anyone done this?<P>Thanks,<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-19-2001||04:19 AM||||The footwell bulbs, domelight bulbs and dash bulbs are all the same.  The bulb # is 914 (you were close).  You can find these at any hardware store and probably your local WalMart, too.  Best of luck trying to find colored bulbs for the ashtrays, etc.  If you do find 'em, let me know as I wouldn't mind having some too.<P>Here's a suggestion for your lights.  If you have 3 switches on your dome light (meaning that you can turn on either your dome light or either side reading light), you might consider just pulling the two bulbs in the center of your dome light.  This way you can turn that on, but really only get footwell lights (as you're driving).  Leave the outer reading lights alone in case you really need to see something.  (Good idea too so you can turn them on in case you get pulled over at night.  Gives the cops a better sense of security.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hartz||09-19-2001||09:06 AM||||One idea for the ashtray lights - or really, any bulbs that you can't find a replacement for:  Try coating it with red nail polish.  It won't be as nice as a pure red bulb, but it will give a redish glow, and should generally match the theme.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||09-19-2001||09:46 PM||||If really want to give the interior that red look when you open the door just install red neon lights.  I did this with my jeep using 4 10" neon tubes and it looks sweet.  I did this because the factory lights don't let you see squat!  The best way to do this is to go to a junkyard and get the factory connectors off another car.  This will allow you to change back to the factory lights with no problem.  As far as attaching the tubes to the interior all you need is some self-stick velcro.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brandon86SE||09-19-2001||10:44 PM||||Alright, it's been done.  The lights in the dome were different from the footwells, from the factory.  However, the footwell lights (194) fit in there, and I ended up doing that approach, since I couldn't find the odd style of the dome lights in a red.  They're a little dimmer, but it still looks good.  Next step: blacklight!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks everyone for the comments!<P>Brandon<P>oh, and Monkeyman, yes I left the push-button lights white, so I can read stuff still (ie. timeslips  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  That was the plan.<BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Brandon86SE (edited 09-19-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||09-20-2001||12:42 AM||||ok, I just took some pics with my digital (sorry, they're a little blurry).  My photoshop isn't working for some reason, so they're still big, resolution wise, but size isn't too bad.  As soon as I figure out what's going on I'll repost them.  For now, this is what it looks like!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Red1(small).jpg"> <BR>Looking in from the back.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Red2(small).jpg"> <BR>Looking in from the front.<P>I think it looks great!  I know I'll be running downstairs to open the door all night long!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brandon<p>[This message has been edited by Brandon86SE (edited 09-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||09-20-2001||10:41 AM||||I have blue 194 bulbs in the footwell, and they used to be in the overhead dome.  I've been thinking of putting blue ones up there too, and seeing how that looks. Also, I bougt some of that thin EL string light stuff from Autozone and ran it on the front firewall just above the carpet.  5' long with transformer is $20.  I don't have these hooked up to the dome lights, these come on when the ignition is on.  Can't see it at day, but looks great at night.  Not as bright as neon tubes (thought about those), but a soft eerie glow coming from the footwells  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I've been thinking of getting another length of it and and running it under the seats.  I will get some pics asap.<P>||||reg||1
